  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.# km of irrigation canals and drainage in disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture (Donggala and Sigi)
2.# of culverts and bridges disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture (Donggala  and Sigi)
3 # local markets rehabilitated or reconstructed
4 # households that benefit from economic infrastructure rehabilitation (men and women), including direct beneficiaries (self-employed; employees) and indirect beneficiaries (consumers/users) &#x2013; in retail and agriculture
5# newly created jobs in the waste management and recycling ecosystem (collection, sorting, processing retailing), direct and indirect, men and women</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Heavily damaged buildings and economic infrastructure caused by the earthquake and government assessment damage and losses has deemed the building as unsafe and unsuitable for use. Hence, we have defined the buildings and beneficiaries as zero although there was a building and there were beneficiaries on the site before the earthquake.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Cumulative 4 km of irrigation canals and drainage in disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture.
2. Cumulative 2 culverts and bridges disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture.
3. Cumulative 3 local market rehabilitated or reconstructed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Achieved - 8 (Eight) community infrastructures related to function of irrigation canals and drainage approved with estimated length of 4 km completed by first semester 2022. 
2. Achieved - 2 subprojects completed. The farmer bridge Belunak in East Lombok was completed in December 2020 and Tuva suspension bridge in Sigi district was completed in April 2021.
3. Achieved - 3 subprojects completed. Genggelang village local market reconstruction has been completed and handed over to the community and formally transfer the asset to GoI. 2 local markets in Central Sulawesi have been reconstructed by the 1st semester 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 4 km of irrigation canals and drainage in disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture.
2. 2 of culverts and bridges disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture.
3. 1 local market rehabilitated or reconstructed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Partially achieved - 6 community infrastructures related to function of irrigation canals and drainage approved with estimated length of 3,1 km; rehabilitation/ reconstruction works is planned to be started in 2nd semester of 2020.
2. Partially achieved &#x2013; Two bridges approved; DEDs are in progress.
3. Partially achieved - Genggelang village local market reconstruction is approved; DED is completed, and construction planned to start in early 2nd semester of 2020.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Cumulative 4 km of irrigation canals and drainage in disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture.
2. Cumulative 2 culverts and bridges disaster-affected areas rehabilitated or reconstructed for improved agriculture.
3. Cumulative 3 local market rehabilitated or reconstructed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Partially achieved - 8 (Eight) community infrastructures related to function of irrigation canals and drainage approved with estimated length of 4 km
2. Achieved - 2 subprojects completed. The farmer bridge Belunak in East Lombok completed in December 2020 and Tuva suspension bridge in Sigi district completed on in April 2021.
3. Partially achieved - 1 of 3 subprojects completed. Genggelang village local market reconstruction has been completed and handed over to the community for immediate utilization while awaiting formal administrative asset transfer to GoI. Remaining rehabilitation of 2 local markets in Central Sulawesi are in ongoing reconstruction process and expected to be completed by early 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
